  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q4",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "The amount of petrol used by a car travelling at a constant speed is directly proportional to the distance travelled. A car uses 6 L of petrol to travel 56 km. How much petrol will be used to travel 140 km at the same speed?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "15 litres",
      "worked": "Let $P$ be the petrol used in litres and $d$ the distance travelled in kilometres.\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=kd\\\\6&=k\\times56\\\\k&=\\frac{6}{56}=\\frac{3}{28}\\\\P&=\\frac{3}{28}d\\\\P&=\\frac{3}{28}\\times140\\\\P&=15\\end{align*}$$\n15 litres of petrol will be used.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
